HTML - HyperText Markup Language.
It tells the computer what things are, and it provides access to the functionality that's already there in the browser.
It only provides structure to the page.

1. Formatting Text in HTML-
Opening tag for para tag is <p> and closing tag for the same is </p>.
Opening tag, content and closing tag together is called an element.

<p>This is paragraph tag.</p>
<h1> headline</h1>
<article>This is an article.</article>

<p>This paragraph has <em>text that's emphasized</em>for effect.</p>
<p> used to tell the browser given section is a paragraph. 

There are 6 headlines, <h1> being the biggest and <h6> is the smallest headline.

For Italics, we have <i> when we only want visual only italics <em> for emphasis on italics. 
For bold, we use <b>, which is visual-only, whereas we use <strong> whenever we want to convey seriousness and urgency to screen readers.

Lists are of 3 kinds ordered <ol>, unoredered lists <ul> and definition lists. <li> stands for list item. Ordered lists have sequence.
Lists which represent key value pairs are known as definition lists and they have <dt> i.e. definition terms and <dd> definition description and <dl> is used to wrap definition list.
Handling dates and times can get tricky in programming languages, not in HTML though. We use <time> element to format a time or date anything that is related to specific moment in time or range that computers can understand.
<time>May 8, 2025</time>
<br />
<time>8 May 2025</time>
